{
  "company_name": "FoodPlan Analytics",
  "industry": "Food & Beverage",
  "use_case": "Scenario planning and business simulation for food product portfolios",
  "space_title": "FoodPlan Analytics - Scenario Planning & Simulation 🎯",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Food & Beverage\n\n**Use case:** Scenario Planning & Business Simulation\n\nFoodPlan Analytics — portfolio scenario planning and pricing simulation across 20 product categories, multiple consumer segments, and retail/foodservice/e-commerce channels. S&OP and Revenue Growth Management teams use this space to stress-test COGS inflation, demand elasticity, and competitive pressure week-to-week; the VP of Strategy and CFO use it to allocate investment, quantify revenue-at-risk, and rank optimal price moves heading into the annual operating plan.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Total simulated revenue ($) — top-line under each scenario set\n- Average simulated margin (%) — contribution margin after COGS shocks\n- Revenue at risk ($) — downside exposure across disruption scenarios\n- Optimal price change (%) — RGM recommendation; CPG elasticity typically -0.3 to -0.6\n- Confidence level (%) — statistical confidence on outcome bands\n- Invest count — categories flagged High investment priority\n- Disruption scenario count — adverse runs in the trailing period\n- Market share (%) — competitive position by segment / channel\n\n**Data sources**\n- `product_categories` — daily simulation runs with scenario type, simulated revenue, margin, price change\n- `scenario_runs` — weekly market conditions with input cost index, consumer sentiment, competitive pressure, elasticity\n- `market_snapshots` — monthly outcomes with expected revenue, revenue-at-risk, optimal price change, investment priority",
  "schema_basename": "fb_scenario_planning",
