  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Scenario Planning & Business Simulation for a multi-category food & beverage portfolio under COGS volatility (commodity inflation, labor, freight), shifting consumer sentiment, and competitive pricing pressure. Stakeholders include the S&OP and Revenue Growth Management leaders (price simulation, demand elasticity), the VP of Strategy (portfolio mix, investment priority), and the CFO (revenue at risk, contribution margin). Scenario_type is Base / Upside / Downside / Disruption; investment_priority is Low / Medium / High / Critical.\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Total simulated revenue = SUM(simulated_revenue_usd); top-line across scenario runs\n- Avg simulated margin = AVG(simulated_margin_pct); CPG healthy contribution margin 25-40%\n- Revenue at risk = SUM(revenue_at_risk_usd); downside scenario exposure\n- Optimal price change = AVG(optimal_price_change_pct); CPG elasticity typically -0.3 to -0.6 (10% price rise → 3-6% volume loss)\n- Confidence level = AVG(confidence_level_pct); statistical band 70-95%\n- Invest count = COUNT(investment_priority IN ('High','Critical'))\n- Disruption count = COUNT(scenario_type='Disruption')\n- Market share = AVG(market_share_pct) on scenario_runs\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - scenario_kpi_monthly (source: product_categories) — dims: run_date, segment, channel, scenario_type; measures: avg_simulated_revenue, avg_simulated_margin, total_simulated_revenue, run_count, disruption_count, total_price_change_percent, unique_category_count, max_simulated_revenue.\n  - portfolio_kpi_monthly (source: market_snapshots) — dims: outcome_month, segment, channel, investment_priority; measures: total_expected_revenue, total_revenue_at_risk, avg_optimal_price_change, avg_confidence, invest_count, unique_category_count, max_expected_revenue.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. category_id, category_name, input_cost_index, consumer_sentiment_index, demand_elasticity).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Show the monthly trend in total revenue at risk across all segments for the trailing 12 months.",
    "Top 10 categories by expected revenue under base scenarios — what is the optimal price change for each?",
    "Which channels show the highest disruption count, and how does that affect average simulated margin?",
    "How has total simulated revenue trended month-over-month across consumer segments?",
    "Top 10 categories flagged High or Critical investment priority — what is the projected revenue uplift?",
    "Which segments have the most negative demand elasticity, and what are the recommended price moves?",
    "What is the monthly trend in average simulated margin, and which scenario types are pulling it down?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in unique categorys?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT run_date, MEASURE(unique_category_count) AS unique_category_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.scenario_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY run_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has highest simulated revenue changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT run_date, MEASURE(max_simulated_revenue) AS max_simulated_revenue",
        "FROM {fqn}.scenario_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY run_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the monthly trend in highest expected revenue?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT outcome_month, MEASURE(max_expected_revenue) AS max_expected_revenue",
        "FROM {fqn}.portfolio_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY outcome_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has invest count changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT outcome_month, MEASURE(invest_count) AS invest_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.portfolio_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY outcome_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total simulated revenue usd over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT run_date, SUM(simulated_revenue_usd) AS total_simulated_revenue_usd",
        "FROM {fqn}.product_categories",
        "GROUP BY run_date ORDER BY run_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total price elasticity of demand over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(demand_elasticity) AS total_demand_elasticity",
        "FROM {fqn}.scenario_runs",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has the average recommended price change pct changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT outcome_month, AVG(optimal_price_change_pct) AS avg_optimal_price_change_pct",
        "FROM {fqn}.market_snapshots",
        "GROUP BY outcome_month ORDER BY outcome_month"
      ]
    }
  ],
